-If you have a bunch of gas spores together, and you kill one, its explosion 
will kill another, which will explode, which kills another, etc. (like 
exploding barrels in DOOM)
-If you have a lit ! of oil, and you throw it, it will explode. If you throw it 
at a gas spore, the explosion will(should) kill it, setting off the chain 
reaction.
-If you have a ! of oil in your inventory, and you are hit with fire, the ! 
will explode.

BUT, if you have a ! of oil on the floor, and you hit it with fire, it will not 
explode. Why not? Maybe it would be too much work (or too unbalancing) to have 
objects on the ground affected by spells, etc. acting on the square they are 
on. Then again, polypiling exists, so...? I think it would be cool, anyway. 
Sort of a low-impact, low-cost land mine. Of course, I also think Malotov 
cocktails should be implemented: (a)pply a mummy wrapping, towel, or blindfold 
to a ! of booze, then chuck it...

